## Experiment

In addition to my main artifact, I was interested in this and decided to use the same prompt through five different AI models to check out how frequently Slop turned up when it was never intended to, and how thoroughly each free model handled the task on its own. 

What I found was that there were errors in three of the five AI models, with the other two completing the task successfully. Take a look at the results below and how subtle or glaring the mistakes are. One AI even cycled to the word CRAP which would most definitely derail a class full of younger elementary-aged students. 

The evaluation prompt used was:
> I need help creating a word ladder. Start with the word Slop and turn it into Care by changing 1 letter at a time.

Errors like this are a good example of what Slop is all about: a confident, plausible-looking final answer, but without much consideration or oversight to the depth behind what is actually being shared.

